            "text": "Most warm mist units are rated somewhere between about 100 and 300 watts. At 280 watts running eight hours a night and 17 cents per kilowatt-hour, that is roughly $11 a month in the worst case. Units with a humidistat cycle the heater off and use less. Ultrasonic cool mist units typically draw 25 to 40 watts."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do warm mist humidifiers make a room warmer?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Not noticeably. The vapor cools within inches of the outlet, and the heat involved is small compared with a space heater. What changes is how the air feels: humid air at the same temperature feels a little warmer to many people than dry air, which is a comfort benefit rather than heating."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Are warm mist humidifiers safe for babies?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Pediatric guidance generally says no. The American Academy of Pediatrics and the Mayo Clinic recommend cool mist humidifiers for children because hot water and steam can cause burns if the unit is tipped or touched. Use a cool mist humidifier in a nursery and keep any warm mist unit out of children's reach."
          }
